VALUES (
  '2026/09/30/hdq-month-september-2026',
  'month', 'month',
  'The Month the US Bond Market Overruled Oil, Gold and the Bank of Canada', 'Brent rose 14% and the Strait of Hormuz stayed shut, yet the TSX, gold and the Canadian dollar all fell as the US 10-year yield crossed 5% for the first time since 2007 and the Federal Reserve raised rates. The Bank of Canada held at 2.25% and watched its own yields rise by 36 basis points.',
  '<ul>
<li><strong>The TSX fell 2.6% in September to close at 35,236,</strong><span> its lowest finish since July 31 and 4.7% below the August 25 record close of 36,957.63, in a month where Brent crude gained 14.4%.</span></li>
<li><strong>The US 10-year Treasury yield crossed 5% for the first time since 2007 and closed at 5.29%,</strong><span> after the Federal Reserve raised its rate 25 basis points on September 16 to 3.75 to 4.00%, the first hike since 2023.</span></li>
<li><strong>The Bank of Canada held at 2.25% on September 2, its seventh straight hold,</strong><span> yet the Government of Canada 2-year and 5-year yields each rose 36 basis points and USD/CAD climbed 2.3% to 1.4188.</span></li>
<li><strong>Gold futures fell 5.5% in the month and 8.2% from the September 3 high,</strong><span> including a 3.5% single-day drop on September 28, the day Washington rejected the Iranian seven-day Hormuz reopening plan.</span></li>
<li><strong>Canada lost 41,700 jobs in August and wage growth slowed to 2.0%,</strong><span> while swap markets priced a 59% chance of a Bank of Canada hike on October 28 and about 100 basis points of hikes over twelve months.</span></li>
</ul>',
  '<style>.mia-lede{font-size:18px;line-height:1.6;color:#15233b}.mia-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:13px;margin:8px 0 14px}@media(max-width:680px){.mia-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}.mia-stat{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e4e7ec;border-top:3px solid #1a3560;padding:15px 15px 13px;border-radius:3px}.mia-stat.g{border-top-color:#e8a825}.mia-stat.u{border-top-color:#3a7a55}.mia-stat.d{border-top-color:#8a3030}.mia-stat .v{font-family:"Bricolage Grotesque",sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:27px;line-height:1;color:#15233b;letter-spacing:-.02em}.mia-stat .v small{font-size:14px;font-weight:700;color:#8b93a0}.mia-stat .l{font-size:11px;color:#6b7280;margin-top:8px;line-height:1.35;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;font-weight:600}.mia-stat .c{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;margin-top:6px}.mia-stat .c.p{color:#3a7a55}.mia-stat .c.n{color:#8a3030}.mia-stat .c.f{color:#7e93b4}.mia-pull{border-left:3px solid #e8a825;padding:6px 0 6px 22px;margin:30px 0;font-family:"Bricolage Grotesque",sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:21px;line-height:1.32;color:#1a3560}.mia-scen{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:14px;margin:14px 0 6px}@media(max-width:760px){.mia-scen{grid-template-columns:1fr}}.mia-card{border:1px solid #e4e7ec;border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden;display:flex;flex-direction:column}.mia-card .t{padding:13px 15px;color:#fff}.mia-card.base .t{background:#1a3560}.mia-card.bull .t{background:#2c5f44}.mia-card.bear .t{background:#6e2a2a}.mia-card .t .nm{font-family:"Bricolage Grotesque",sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:16px}.mia-card .t .pr{font-size:11px;opacity:.82;margin-top:2px}.mia-card .bd{padding:13px 15px;font-size:13.5px;flex:1}.mia-card .bd p{margin-bottom:9px}.mia-card .tr{border-top:1px solid #e4e7ec;padding:11px 15px;background:#f7f8fa}.mia-card .tr .lb{font-size:9.5px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b7280;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:6px}.mia-card .tr ul{list-style:none;font-size:12px;margin:0;padding:0}.mia-card .tr li{padding:3px 0;color:#15233b}.mia-card .tr li:before{content:"\25B8 ";color:#c98e16}.mia-tbl-w{overflow-x:auto;border:1px solid #e4e7ec;border-radius:4px;margin:14px 0}.mia-tbl{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:12.5px;min-width:600px}.mia-tbl th,.mia-tbl td{padding:8px 12px;text-align:right;border-bottom:1px solid #eef1f5;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.mia-tbl th{background:#1a3560;color:#fff;font-weight:600;font-size:11px}.mia-tbl th:first-child,.mia-tbl td:first-child{text-align:left}.mia-tbl td.na{color:#c8cdd5}</style><p class="mia-lede">September began with a war and ended with a bond market. Brent crude rose 14% in the month, the Federal Reserve raised its policy rate for the first time since 2023, the Bank of Canada held for a seventh consecutive meeting, and the Strait of Hormuz stayed closed to normal traffic for a seventh month. The TSX still fell 2.6%, the Canadian dollar fell 2.3% and gold fell 5.5%. All three moves line up against the same variable, and it is not oil. It is the US 10-year Treasury yield, which crossed 5% for the first time since 2007 and closed the month at 5.29%.</p><h2 id="glance" data-toc="The Month at a Glance" data-toc-n="01"><span class="ix" style="font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#c98e16;letter-spacing:.1em;display:block;margin-bottom:8px;text-transform:uppercase;">Section 01</span>The Month at a Glance</h2><div class="mia-grid"><div class="mia-stat d"><div class="v">35,236</div><div class="l">TSX close, Sep 30</div><div class="c n">-2.6% in September; high 36,633 (Sep 3)</div></div><div class="mia-stat u"><div class="v"><small>US$</small>103.53</div><div class="l">Brent crude, Sep 30</div><div class="c p">+14.4% in September; peak 108.75 (Sep 15)</div></div><div class="mia-stat u"><div class="v"><small>US$</small>90.42</div><div class="l">WTI crude, Sep 30</div><div class="c p">+5.4% in September; peak 102.48 (Sep 10)</div></div><div class="mia-stat d"><div class="v"><small>US$</small>4,235</div><div class="l">Gold futures, Sep 30</div><div class="c n">-5.5% in September; low 4,168 (Sep 28)</div></div><div class="mia-stat d"><div class="v">3.99<small>%</small></div><div class="l">GoC 10-year yield, Sep 29</div><div class="c n">+26 bps in September</div></div><div class="mia-stat d"><div class="v">0.7048</div><div class="l">CAD/USD, Sep 29</div><div class="c n">-2.3% in September; USD/CAD 1.4188</div></div><div class="mia-stat "><div class="v">2.25<small>%</small></div><div class="l">Bank of Canada rate</div><div class="c f">held Sep 2; 7th consecutive hold</div></div><div class="mia-stat "><div class="v">3.75<small>-4.00%</small></div><div class="l">Fed funds rate</div><div class="c f">raised 25 bps Sep 16; first hike since 2023</div></div></div><p>Eight numbers, and the two with the least apparent connection are the ones that explain the rest. The Bank of Canada did not move its rate at all, yet its 2-year and 5-year yields rose 36 basis points each. Oil rose by an amount that would normally lift a Canadian equity index and a Canadian dollar, and both fell. The variable that changed the most was neither a central bank decision nor a barrel of crude. It was the price of long-dated US government debt, and by the final session of the month it had carried the 10-year Treasury yield to 5.29% and the 30-year to 5.64%.</p><h2 id="arc" data-toc="The Arc of the Month" data-toc-n="02"><span class="ix" style="font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#c98e16;letter-spacing:.1em;display:block;margin-bottom:8px;text-transform:uppercase;">Section 02</span>The Arc of the Month</h2><p>The month opened under the weight of the last week of August. US strikes on Larak Island on August 30 and Iranian retaliation had taken the TSX to 36,180.72 on August 31, already 2.1% below the August 25 record close of 36,957.63. The index fell another 1.0% on September 1, to 35,825.73, as tanker attacks in the Strait of Hormuz returned the war premium to oil.</p><p>The first week then turned on the Bank of Canada and a jobs report. The Bank held at 2.25% on September 2 and its governor said it stood ready to raise more than once if energy inflation persisted. The TSX rose 0.74% that day and 1.50% on September 3, to 36,633.12, the highest close of the month and 0.9% below the record. On September 4 Statistics Canada reported a loss of 41,700 jobs in August against a consensus gain of about 15,000, with average wage growth slowing to 2.0%, the slowest pace in nine years. US payrolls the same day added 162,000 against an expected 53,000.</p><p>The second week was the tanker war. Canada''s retaliatory tariffs on $27.6 billion of US goods took effect on September 8, the Saudi-flagged tanker Sidr had been struck with the loss of two crew, and Houthi forces hit three Saudi Aramco sites. On September 10 the Saudi East-West pipeline, the main bypass around Hormuz, was struck and shut. WTI closed at US$102.48 that day and Brent at US$107.63. The TSX lost 1.11% on the same session, to 35,506.30. Brent peaked at US$108.75 on September 15.</p><p>The third week belonged to the Federal Reserve. On September 16 it raised its target range 25 basis points to 3.75 to 4.00%, by unanimous vote, with 16 of 18 officials projecting at least one more hike before year end. The TSX closed that day at 35,491.30, the low of the month to that point. It rebounded 1.08% the next day as Treasury yields retreated, reached 36,335.61 on September 22 on reports that President Trump was open to meeting Iranian President Pezeshkian at the UN General Assembly, and then lost 584.18 points on September 23, its worst session in more than three months, as copper, gold and silver reversed and the US 10-year yield rose 15 basis points to 5.11%.</p><p>The last week was a bond market story. Iran offered to reopen the Strait within seven days, conditional on eased US military pressure. On September 28 Washington rejected the plan and demanded that nuclear terms come first. Gold futures fell 3.5% in that single session, to US$4,168.40, and the TSX fell 0.87%. The 10-year Treasury yield passed 5.2%. On September 30 core PCE inflation came in at 3.0% against 3.3% expected, and the odds of an October Fed hike fell from about 71% on September 29 to about 37% by the morning of September 30, on two different trackers. The front end of the Treasury curve priced the soft print. The 30-year yield did not: it rose to 5.64%. The TSX closed the month at 35,235.90.</p><p>The TSX closed September 2.6% lower, and the path was a decline through the tanker war, a partial recovery after the Fed decision and a second slide through the bond market selloff of the final week.</p><div class="hdq-chart"><div style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #d0d0d0;width:100%;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;"><div style="background:#f5f5f5;border-bottom:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:10px 14px;display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;"><span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#111;letter-spacing:0.02em;">S&amp;P/TSX COMPOSITE</span><span style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700;color:#111;">35,236</span><span style="font-size:13px;color:#c0392b;">&#9660; -2.6% IN SEPTEMBER</span><span style="font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-left:auto;">Daily close &nbsp;|&nbsp; Sep 1-30, 2026</span></div><div style="padding:12px 14px 8px;"><script>(function(){
var _cs = document.currentScript;
var NS = "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", F = "-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif";
function el(tag, attrs, txt){ var e = document.createElementNS(NS, tag); for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]); if (txt !== undefined) e.textContent = txt; return e; }
function tw(s, fs, up){ return Math.ceil(String(s).length * fs * (up ? 0.68 : 0.58)); }
function fmt(v, ty){ if (ty == "int") return Math.round(v).toLocaleString("en-US"); if (ty == "pct2") return v.toFixed(2) + "%"; if (ty == "usd") return "$" + Math.round(v); if (ty == "usd0") return "$" + Math.round(v).toLocaleString("en-US"); return String(Math.round(v)); }
function niceTicks(lo, hi, target){ var raw = (hi - lo) / target, mag = Math.pow(10, Math.floor(Math.log(raw) / Math.LN10)), steps = [1, 2, 2.5, 5, 10], st = mag, i; for (i = 0; i < steps.length; i++){ st = steps[i] * mag; if (st >= raw) break; } var a = Math.floor(lo / st) * st, b = Math.ceil(hi / st) * st, out = [], v; for (v = a; v <= b + st * 0.001; v += st) out.push(Math.round(v * 1000) / 1000); return out; }
function draw(C){
  var W = 680, H = 300, margin = {left: 62, right: 24, top: 18, bottom: 46};
  var PW = W - margin.left - margin.right, PH = H - margin.top - margin.bottom, n = C.dates.length;
  var svg = document.createElementNS(NS, "svg");
  svg.setAttribute("viewBox", "0 0 680 300");
  svg.setAttribute("width", "100%");
  svg.setAttribute("preserveAspectRatio", "xMidYMid meet");
  var vals = [], si, i;
  C.series.forEach(function(s){ s.data.forEach(function(x){ vals.push(x); }); });
  (C.refs || []).forEach(function(r){ vals.push(r.v); });
  var mn = Math.min.apply(null, vals), mx = Math.max.apply(null, vals), pad = (mx - mn) * 0.1;
  var ticks = niceTicks(mn - pad, mx + pad, 5);
  var lo = ticks[0], hi = ticks[ticks.length - 1];
  function xp(k){ return margin.left + PW * (k / (n - 1)); }
  function yp(v){ return margin.top + PH - PH * ((v - lo) / (hi - lo)); }
  /* 1 gridlines */
  ticks.forEach(function(t){ var yy = yp(t); svg.appendChild(el("line", {x1: margin.left, x2: margin.left + PW, y1: yy, y2: yy, stroke: "#ececec", "stroke-width": 0.5})); svg.appendChild(el("text", {x: margin.left - 6, y: yy + 3, "text-anchor": "end", "font-family": F, "font-size": 8.5, fill: "#aaa"}, fmt(t, C.fmt))); });
  /* event bands */
  (C.bands || []).forEach(function(b){ var x1 = xp(b.a), x2 = xp(b.b); svg.appendChild(el("rect", {x: x1, y: margin.top, width: x2 - x1, height: PH, fill: b.color, "fill-opacity": b.op})); });
  /* 2 reference lines */
  (C.refs || []).forEach(function(r){ var ry = yp(r.v); svg.appendChild(el("line", {x1: margin.left, x2: margin.left + PW, y1: ry, y2: ry, stroke: r.color, "stroke-width": 1, "stroke-dasharray": "3,3"})); });
  /* 3 series */
  C.series.forEach(function(s){ var d = s.data.map(function(v, k){ return (k ? "L" : "M") + xp(k).toFixed(1) + " " + yp(v).toFixed(1); }).join(" "); svg.appendChild(el("path", {d: d, fill: "none", stroke: s.color, "stroke-width": s.width || 2, "stroke-dasharray": s.dash || "none", "stroke-linejoin": "round", "stroke-linecap": "round"})); });
  /* 4 axis */
  svg.appendChild(el("line", {x1: margin.left, x2: margin.left + PW, y1: margin.top + PH, y2: margin.top + PH, stroke: "#d8d8d8", "stroke-width": 1}));
  /* 5 endpoint dots and event marker lines */
  C.series.forEach(function(s){ svg.appendChild(el("circle", {cx: xp(n - 1), cy: yp(s.data[n - 1]), r: 3.5, fill: s.color})); });
  (C.events || []).forEach(function(ev){ var ex = xp(ev.i); svg.appendChild(el("line", {x1: ex, x2: ex, y1: margin.top, y2: margin.top + PH, stroke: "#1a3560", "stroke-opacity": 0.4, "stroke-dasharray": "2,3", "stroke-width": 1})); });
  /* 6 pill */
  var pill = C.pill, pillText = pill.text, lastX = xp(n - 1), lastY = yp(C.series[pill.si].data[n - 1]);
  var pillW = tw(pillText, 9, pill.up) + 10, pillH = 16, pillX = lastX - pillW - 6, pillY = lastY - pillH / 2 + (pill.dy || 0);
  if (pillX < margin.left) pillX = margin.left;
  if (pillY < margin.top) pillY = margin.top + 2;
  if (pillY + pillH > margin.top + PH) pillY = margin.top + PH - pillH - 2;
  svg.appendChild(el("rect", {x: pillX, y: pillY, width: pillW, height: pillH, rx: 2, fill: "#e8a825"}));
  svg.appendChild(el("text", {x: pillX + pillW / 2, y: pillY + pillH / 2 + 3.5, "text-anchor": "middle", "font-family": F, "font-size": 9, "font-weight": 700, fill: "#111"}, pillText));
  /* 7 labels and annotations */
  for (i = 0; i < n; i++){ if (i % 3 != 0 && i != n - 1) continue; svg.appendChild(el("text", {x: xp(i), y: margin.top + PH + 15, "text-anchor": "middle", "font-family": F, "font-size": 8, fill: "#999"}, C.dates[i])); }
  (C.bands || []).forEach(function(b){ var x1 = xp(b.a), x2 = xp(b.b); svg.appendChild(el("text", {x: (x1 + x2) / 2, y: margin.top + 11, "text-anchor": "middle", "font-family": F, "font-size": 7, "font-weight": 700, fill: b.lcolor}, b.label)); });
  (C.refs || []).forEach(function(r){ if (!r.label) return; svg.appendChild(el("text", {x: margin.left + 10, y: r.below ? yp(r.v) + 12 : yp(r.v) - 10, "text-anchor": "start", "font-family": F, "font-size": 7, "font-weight": 700, fill: r.lcolor}, r.label)); });
  (C.events || []).forEach(function(ev){
    var ex = xp(ev.i), labelWidth = 0;
    ev.t.forEach(function(L){ labelWidth = Math.max(labelWidth, tw(L, 7, true)); });
    var crowded = C.events.some(function(o){ return o.i !== ev.i && Math.abs(xp(o.i) - ex) < 85; });
    var nearRight = (ex + labelWidth + 3) > (margin.left + PW);
    var offset = (crowded || nearRight) ? -3 : 3;
    var anchor = (crowded || nearRight) ? "end" : "start";
    var yStart = margin.top + 26 + (ev.dy || 0);
    ev.t.forEach(function(L, li){ svg.appendChild(el("text", {x: ex + offset, y: yStart + li * 9, "text-anchor": anchor, "font-family": F, "font-size": 7, "font-weight": 700, fill: "#1a3560"}, L)); });
  });
  var offs = C.labelOffsets || [];
  C.series.forEach(function(s, k){ if (!s.label) return; svg.appendChild(el("text", {x: xp(n - 1) - 4, y: yp(s.data[n - 1]) + 3 + (offs[k] || 0), "text-anchor": "end", "font-family": F, "font-size": 7.5, "font-weight": 700, fill: s.color}, s.label)); });
  (C.notes || []).forEach(function(a){ svg.appendChild(el("text", {x: xp(a.i), y: yp(a.v) + a.dy, "text-anchor": a.anchor, "font-family": F, "font-size": 8, "font-weight": 700, fill: a.fill}, a.t)); });
  _cs.parentNode.appendChild(svg);
}
draw({"dates":["Sep 1","Sep 2","Sep 3","Sep 4","Sep 8","Sep 9","Sep 10","Sep 11","Sep 14","Sep 15","Sep 16","Sep 17","Sep 18","Sep 21","Sep 22","Sep 23","Sep 24","Sep 25","Sep 28","Sep 29","Sep 30"],"fmt":"int","bands":[{"a":4,"b":10,"color":"#c0392b","op":0.05,"label":"TANKER WAR SELLOFF","lcolor":"#8a3030"}],"refs":[{"v":36957.63,"color":"#2e7d32","label":"AUG 25 RECORD CLOSE 36,958","lcolor":"#2e7d32","below":true}],"events":[{"i":1,"t":["BoC holds","Sep 2"]},{"i":10,"t":["Fed hikes","Sep 16"]},{"i":15,"t":["-584 pts","Sep 23"]},{"i":18,"t":["Hormuz plan","rejected"]}],"series":[{"data":[35825.73,36091.61,36633.12,36513.8,36123.1,35906.56,35506.3,35697.5,35702.5,35582.07,35491.3,35874.26,35806.65,36009.4,36335.61,35751.43,35706.46,35800.89,35489.86,35460.3,35235.9],"color":"#4a5568","width":2.4}],"pill":{"si":0,"text":"35,236"}});
})();</script></div><div style="font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10px;color:#999;padding:4px 14px 10px;font-style:italic;">Source: Yahoo Finance, S&amp;P/TSX Composite (^GSPTSE) daily close, Sep 1-30, 2026. &nbsp;|&nbsp; hdq.ca</div></div></div><p style="font-size:11px;color:#666;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;margin-top:6px;">The TSX through September. The shaded span marks the September 8 to 16 slide through the tanker war and the Federal Reserve decision; the dashed line is the August 25 record close. September 7 was Labour Day and the market was closed.</p><p>The remainder of this report isolates the five patterns inside that arc. Each became visible only across the full twenty-one sessions, and each carries a specific implication for the October 2 payrolls report, the October 19 CPI release and the October 28 decisions of both central banks.</p><h2 id="p1" data-toc="Canadian Borrowing Costs Followed the US Long End, Not the Bank of Canada" data-toc-n="P1" data-toc-sub="1"><span class="ix" style="font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#c98e16;letter-spacing:.1em;display:block;margin-bottom:8px;text-transform:uppercase;">Pattern One</span>Canadian Borrowing Costs Followed the US Long End, Not the Bank of Canada</h2><p class="mia-lede">The Bank of Canada policy rate did not change in September. The Government of Canada 2-year yield rose from 3.01% to 3.37%, the 5-year from 3.33% to 3.69% and the 10-year from 3.73% to 3.99%, and USD/CAD rose on fifteen consecutive daily observations, from 1.3784 on September 8 to 1.4188 on September 29. The currency and the yield curve repriced without the central bank doing anything.</p><p>The timing of the large moves points to the US long end, not to either central bank. On September 16 the Federal Reserve raised its rate, and the Canadian 10-year yield fell 3 basis points that day and another 9 the next, to 3.83%, as US Treasury yields retreated from their post-decision spike. On September 23, with no central bank event, the US 10-year yield rose 15 basis points and the Canadian 10-year rose 13, to 3.96%. The spread between the two 10-year yields widened from 100 to 128 basis points between August 28 and September 28, and 19 of those 28 basis points arrived after the Fed hike.</p><p>Bank of Canada yields did respond to one domestic event. The 2-year yield rose 10 basis points on September 2, the day of the hold, because the Bank said it could hike more than once. The 2-year then rose another 26 basis points through September 14 as oil climbed, and 15 of that came on September 10 alone. The front end of the Canadian curve moved on inflation risk. The long end and the currency moved on Treasuries.</p><div class="mia-pull">The Bank of Canada held at 2.25% all month. Its 5-year yield, the one that prices a fixed mortgage, rose 36 basis points anyway.</div><p>The 2-year, 5-year and 10-year yields rose together through the month, with the largest step on the oil surge of September 10 and a second on the US yield jump of September 23, and with a decline on the day after the Fed hike.</p><div class="hdq-chart"><div style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #d0d0d0;width:100%;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;"><div style="background:#f5f5f5;border-bottom:1px solid #d0d0d0;padding:10px 14px;display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;"><span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#111;letter-spacing:0.02em;">GOC BENCHMARK YIELDS</span><span style="font-size:20px;font-weight:700;color:#111;">3.99%</span><span style="font-size:13px;color:#2e7d32;">&#9650; +26 BPS 10Y IN SEPTEMBER</span><span style="font-size:11px;color:#888;margin-left:auto;">Daily &nbsp;|&nbsp; Aug 31-Sep 29, 2026</span></div><div style="padding:12px 14px 8px;"><script>(function(){
var _cs = document.currentScript;
var NS = "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", F = "-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif";
function el(tag, attrs, txt){ var e = document.createElementNS(NS, tag); for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]); if (txt !== undefined) e.textContent = txt; return e; }
function tw(s, fs, up){ return Math.ceil(String(s).length * fs * (up ? 0.68 : 0.58)); }
function fmt(v, ty){ if (ty == "int") return Math.round(v).toLocaleString("en-US"); if (ty == "pct2") return v.toFixed(2) + "%"; if (ty == "usd") return "$" + Math.round(v); if (ty == "usd0") return "$" + Math.round(v).toLocaleString("en-US"); return String(Math.round(v)); }
function niceTicks(lo, hi, target){ var raw = (hi - lo) / target, mag = Math.pow(10, Math.floor(Math.log(raw) / Math.LN10)), steps = [1, 2, 2.5, 5, 10], st = mag, i; for (i = 0; i < steps.length; i++){ st = steps[i] * mag; if (st >= raw) break; } var a = Math.floor(lo / st) * st, b = Math.ceil(hi / st) * st, out = [], v; for (v = a; v <= b + st * 0.001; v += st) out.push(Math.round(v * 1000) / 1000); return out; }
function draw(C){
  var W = 680, H = 300, margin = {left: 62, right: 24, top: 18, bottom: 46};
